  "repair": [
    "Grants pin the canonical root device/inode at activation. Relative native directory handles retain authorized ancestors and targets across read/create operations; logical identity is checked before publishing results.",
    "macOS O_SEARCH and Linux O_PATH keep execute-only ancestors usable. Listing opens a separate read handle on demand; bounded batches retain the configured maximum.",
    "Windows uses parent-relative NtCreateFile and handle-owned NtQueryDirectoryFile through Koffi; no path-based listing or mkdir fallback. Reparse points and malformed records fail closed.",
    "Cancellation does not close a native object while a consumer still uses it. Late opens are closed, worker termination releases owned directory descriptors, and cleanup errors remain observable.",
    "Native package family version0.1.3 adds the public directory subpath and is required by the browser provider. No package was published."
  ],
